keel-pve (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The index signature is also trusted from the images keyring,
    /usr/share/keyrings/keel-images-keyring.gpg, when the file is there
    (handbook decision 0055). sqv gets the main keyring and the images
    keyring as 2 files, never merged, and needs 1 good signature by a key
    of either file. keel-archive-keyring 0.3.0 and later installs the
    images keyring. Before 0.3.0, keel-pve verifies with the main keyring
    alone, as before.
  * The index is still signed by the main key. An index signed by the
    main key and the images key together verifies with the main keyring
    alone, so the publisher can add the images signature before every
    host has the images keyring.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

keel-pve (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * keel-pve is published in trixie-testing only, so the README's
    Suites: trixie left apt install keel-pve with "Unable to locate
    package". The README now gives trixie-testing, until the package is
    promoted to trixie. Every subcommand prints a hint on stderr, the
    file /etc/apt/sources.list.d/keel.sources and its deb822 block, when
    no apt source in sources.list or sources.list.d (*.list, *.sources)
    names https://archive.keellinux.org; exit statuses are unchanged.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

keel-pve (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release. keel-pve update fetches aplinfo.dat.gz and
    aplinfo.dat.asc from releases.keellinux.org/pve, verifies the
    signature with sqv against keel-archive-keyring the way pveam does,
    and stores the index under /var/lib/keel-pve only when it verifies
    and every record parses. keel-pve available lists it, keel-pve
    download STORAGE TEMPLATE writes a template into the path pvesm path
    gives for STORAGE:vztmpl/<file>, under the index's file name, renamed
    into place only after its sha512 matched, and keel-pve list shows the
    Keel templates already in the vztmpl storages. A template is written
    into a mktemp directory, never through a planted symlink; a Location
    must be https; curl has connect and transfer time limits and the lock
    a bounded wait. /etc/apt/preferences.d/keel-pve pins every package of
    the Keel archive at -1 except keel-pve and keel-archive-keyring.
    keel-pve-update.timer runs update daily and is shipped disabled. No
    pve-manager file is touched.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
